The E5 q8_1 mat-vec arm: the Q4_K x Q8_1 dot product reached without a dot
instruction, onto f280b26983ad0fdb705a0d9ebf0503e76f2899b0 after the eight-patch
production series. The manual int24 GLSL this patch carries is E5-M, the lane's
negative control; E5-S0 and E5-S1 reach the same dot product through
GL_EXT_integer_dot_product and are what the lane now measures against it.

RADV reports VK_KHR_shader_integer_dot_product functional and every
integerDotProduct*Accelerated bit false on RAVEN2, and ggml-vulkan.cpp gates one
bool named integer_dot_product on integerDotProduct4x8BitPackedSignedAccelerated
alone, so the pinned build compiles no _q8_1 mat-vec pipeline and the whole Q4_K
trunk streams through the FP16 dequantize-then-dot family.

That one bool carries four separable claims, and this patch names each of them,
because an environment variable that moves a field spelled after hardware
acceleration states something about the silicon that stays false:

    integer_dot_functional          the extension is present and its
                                    shaderIntegerDotProduct feature is true; the
                                    driver alone writes it, and it decides which
                                    property struct is chained and whether the
                                    device extension is enabled
    integer_dot_accelerated         integerDotProduct4x8BitPackedSignedAccelerated
                                    verbatim from the driver; nothing in this
                                    build writes it, so every advertised Vulkan
                                    acceleration property reads what RADV reported
    integer_dot_software_lowered    this build computes the packed dot without a
                                    dot instruction, by the replacement GLSL here
                                    or by the driver expanding OpSDotKHR;
                                    GGML_VK_FORCE_INTEGER_DOT=1 writes this field
                                    and only this field
    integer_dot_pipeline_selected   accelerated or software lowered, which the
                                    q8_1 pipeline table, the flash-attention MMQ
                                    selection, and every quantize_y dispatch read

Where the arm is unarmed the selection equals the pinned build's own flag, so the
split renames the pinned behavior rather than changing it.

E5-M's own shader: mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl gains dot_packed_4x8_int24 under
GGML_VK_INT24_DOT, which biases both operands into 0..255 and removes the bias
once per call through sum((au-128)*(bu-128)) = sum(au*bu) - 128*(sum au + sum bu)
+ 65536, and a macro puts it behind the extension's own spelling so all forty
call sites read the same. The Q4_K and Q5_K mmvq_dot_product specializes further:
repack4 masks its quant bytes to 0..15, and Q5_K merges one bit above that, so
only the activation byte needs the bias and the correction rides two accumulators
over sixteen values as one shift. Those sixteen products are written straight-line
with literal shifts and literal masks, the way the pinned function writes four
explicit dot calls, so the module holds sixteen multiplies of constant-masked
bytes and indexes the quant vector statically: the compiled Q4_K variant reaches
46 OpIMul against the extension branch's 30 and the same 73 OpAccessChain. The
FP32 tail is byte-identical to the pinned function, so the replacement is exact
against dotPacked4x8EXT rather than approximate: a C model of both forms agrees
with the signed reference over the whole single-lane domain and four million
random word pairs. mul_mat_vecq.comp requires GL_EXT_integer_dot_product under
the opposite branch of the same define, so the arm compiles on a glslc that
rejects the extension.

That control's measured cost is why it is a control:
evidence/raven2-vulkan-kernel-census/e5/E5-M/ records ACO emitting 224
v_mul_u32_u24_sdwa products and zero v_mad_u32_u24, since SDWA byte select rides
VOP2 on GFX9 while the multiply-add is VOP3 and the two encodings cannot share an
instruction, and the extension form of the same shader compiles to 1328 VALU
against this one's 1646.

GGML_VULKAN_INT24_DOT is a CMake option that reaches both the backend and
vulkan-shaders-gen through the forwarding the extension probes already use, and
both derive GGML_VULKAN_MMVQ_Q8_1_SHADERS from it, so a definition that lands on
one side alone fails at link on arr_dmmv_q4_k_q8_1_f32_data rather than at device
creation. The MMQ and flash-attention int8 shaders have no replacement and keep
reading GGML_VULKAN_INTEGER_DOT_GLSLC_SUPPORT; where they are absent,
ggml_vk_get_mul_mat_mat_pipeline finds an empty pipeline set and clears
quantize_y, so the mat-mat and flash-attention paths stay on the production shape
and E5-M changes the mat-vec alone. An E5-S build compiled by an
extension-capable toolchain admits those families too, which the lane's README
registers as the wider dispatch set that arm carries.

GGML_VK_FORCE_INTEGER_DOT=1 admits that mat-vec on a device reporting no
acceleration. It is read once per process, requires an exact "1", and reaches the
software-lowered field and the info line the same way, so one binary runs both
arms and the control is that binary with the variable unset.
remote/radv-low-priority-env.sh scrubs the variable under every serving profile;
QWEN_FORCE_INTEGER_DOT carries it past that scrub for a served arm that keeps
low-async's own submission shape.
